  "anti_overread": [
    "The mathematical content of these theorems is standard — descent through a finite quotient, idempotent saturation, the Kullback–Leibler decomposition, finite cycle/cochain duality, the universal property of the image factorization, and so on — and is not claimed as novel The paper does not prove a universal exact-six theorem, a universal six-symbol algebra, a unique decomposition theorem, an empirical realization claim, or complete same-level self-certification.",
    "The introduction states the gap that the calculus closes, lists what the paper proves and what it does not prove, and gives a reader's map of the remaining sections.",
    "the present paper supplies the finite calculus that records them in a single typed framework with explicit admissibility, audit, status, and nonclaim discipline.",
    "a finite nonclaim register N that records the negative boundary of every admissible claim.",
    "the full nonclaim register is recorded in Section 16.",
    "The paper does not assert that every phenomenon, every theory, or all of mathematics reduces to six primitives. The calculus accepts a directed-cell judgment P_ i P_ j only under the per-cell admissibility predicate and per-cell profile of Subsection 4.3, and does not assert that every mathematical structure is decomposable into the six primitives.",
    "The paper does not assert that the four model families — PICA, Cantor, abstract interpretation, and graph/cohomology — realize the entire calculus or supply universal theorem sources.",
    "The paper does not assert that any instrument certifies its own complete soundness at the same level, nor that the calculus admits a final self-certifying instrument on a finite tower."
  ],
